{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Is it a small thing that you have brought us up.</b> Corresponding to what Moses began to say to them, 'Is it a small thing for you that you were separated,' they said, 'Is it a small thing that you have brought us up' — that is, the matter is a light thing that you brought us up from a land flowing with milk and honey, which is Egypt; and one who comes from there to the land of Canaan is 'going up,' for it is in the south of the land of Israel." "<b>That you lord it over us — also exercise lordship.</b> That is: you brought us up from Egypt in order to lord over us many lordships. Or one may say that he doubled the lordship to indicate from this the rule of kingship for Moses and the rule of priesthood for Aaron, and the rest of the lordships and prerogatives of the sons of Levi and the sons of Kehath, and also the chieftainship of Elitzaphan son of Uzziel — all of them are included in the word גם ('also'), which is inclusive."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:02.002374871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}